OL,3,GNEWSAThe 260-year-old pub that has
OL,4,Abecome a 'disgrace'
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe agent marketing the privately owned
OL,7,Fsite said it had attracted "a lot of
OL,8,Finterest", adding that an alternative
OL,9,Ffuture for the former public house was
OL,10,F"likely".
OL,12,F"Someone's got to do something about
OL,13,Fit, it's just a disgrace the way it is
OL,14,Fnow," said Roland Leaf, who lives in a
OL,15,Fneighbouring property.
